<title>MEXICO: Mexico coffee exports drop sharply May vs May '96.</title>
<headline>Mexico coffee exports drop sharply May vs May '96.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico exported 270,214 60-kg bags of coffee in May 1997 compared to 458,195 bags in May 1996, the Mexican Coffee Council said Monday.</p>
<p>The council, the country's umbrella organization, said exports so far (October-May) in this 1996-1997 cycle have totaled 3,973,339 bags.  </p>
<p>A full breakdown of the Mexican exports follows in table form. Figures are for 60-kg bags.</p>
<p>    Month     1996-1997	 1995-1996	    1994-1995</p>
<p>    October    163,489	   101,912		 59,303</p>
<p>    November   320,842	   296,510		131,767</p>
<p>    December   390,111	   421,445		260,081</p>
<p>    January    871,321	   745,428		586,669</p>
<p>    February   837,812	   742,815		460,060</p>
<p>    March	671,570	   631,513		603,537</p>
<p>    April	447,980	   529,015		243,772</p>
<p>    May	  270,214	   458,195		287,238</p>
<p>    June	   N/A	     193,293		217,951</p>
<p>    July	   N/A	     219,432		121,033</p>
<p>    August	 N/A	     146,745		184,466</p>
<p>    September    N/A		92,554		101,867</p>
<p>    Total    3,973,339	 4,578,857		  ----</p>
<p>(NB Figures have been revised and updated from previous months)</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530)) E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
